> 
> What I found confusing - A chaotic getting crowned will get
> Stormbringer unless it already exists.  If it already exists you
> get a blessed rustproof +1 runesword (or is it broadsword as
> the alternate?).  You get a "good" weapon either way.  But a
> neutral doesn't get a weapon either way.
> 
> Playing a wizard there's a way to get the weapon at crowning -
> Have the book in your open inventory when praying.

Last time i tried that, it also worked for the Monk (even more useful,
as the spellbook they receive is spectacularly worthless).

IIRC, if you're not liable to receive a weapon gift upon crowning,
your deity will instead bless and rustproof your wielded weapon,
enchant it by one point, unless +1 or better already, and "unrestrict"
it - if you're restricted in the weapon's skill, you can at least
reach "basic" now. That also has some potential for Monks ...

